# LICENSE / CREDIT

This project (`fixll`) is a wrapper around the prebuilt `VERSION.dll` shim plus
an installer script.

The shim is derived from **FuckBootStrap** by sst311212:
  https://github.com/sst311212/FuckBootStrap

FuckBootStrap provides the `bootStrap` compatibility approach (a Detours
`LoadLibraryW` hook that adjusts the KiriKiri `bootStrap` check patterns). All
credit for the core approach goes to sst311212.

Modifications made here (in `src/dllmain.cpp` and `src/VERSION.def`):
  - export forwarders marked `extern "C"` so the `.def` aliases match exactly
    (no C++ name mangling, which previously resolved exports to import stubs)
  - `VERSION.def` has no `LIBRARY` line and is passed directly to the linker
    (the build does NOT use `-lversion`, which aliased exports to stubs)
  - real implementation of the version APIs
    (`GetFileVersionInfoSizeW` / `GetFileVersionInfoW` / `VerQueryValueW`) that
    read the PE version resource directly, instead of forwarding to builtins

No claim of originality over the approach is made. Use at your own risk.
